{
    "word": "sennight",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "7ef50c6c-fdaf-351e-8810-0dcf56b3f963",
                "word": "sennight",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "f0eeb5ae-37ce-441d-815c-7bbcd6fd22c5",
                        "entry_id": "7ef50c6c-fdaf-351e-8810-0dcf56b3f963",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "sennights"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "13be5f99-8456-3ed2-b95a-2203aafc97f2",
                        "entry_id": "7ef50c6c-fdaf-351e-8810-0dcf56b3f963",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A period of seven consecutive days and nights; a week."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "obsolete",
                            "poetic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8002492-765e-4d23-9864-ddffe0f4aa6e",
                                "sense_id": "13be5f99-8456-3ed2-b95a-2203aafc97f2",
                                "text": "I dranke not this sennet / A draught to my pay; / Elynour, I thé pray, / Of thyne ale let vs assay, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "cda53a1d-ec50-4e9e-95f1-cf948757bed6",
                                "sense_id": "13be5f99-8456-3ed2-b95a-2203aafc97f2",
                                "text": "Marry he trots hard vvith a yong maid, betvveen the contract of her marriage, and the day it is ſolemnizd: if the interim be but a ſennight, Times pace is ſo hard, that it ſeemes the length of ſeuen yeare."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bc3c4a6d-2733-4823-94df-4e28e6db2455",
                                "sense_id": "13be5f99-8456-3ed2-b95a-2203aafc97f2",
                                "text": "I was not bit enough to stand up to Edward personally, so I had to console the sufferer by allowing him to grease the wheels of the donkey-cart—a luscious treat that had been specially reserved for me, a sennight past, by the gardener's boy, for putting in a good word on his behalf with the new kitchen-maid."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "533fc67a-3aa4-46fe-9ae7-f39b74fa1711",
                                "sense_id": "13be5f99-8456-3ed2-b95a-2203aafc97f2",
                                "text": "Old woman, what was it the village Elders said a se'nnight since? Eh? Stir your memory."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c0d9f480-c8f3-35e2-a0ce-cb216f515b65",
                        "entry_id": "7ef50c6c-fdaf-351e-8810-0dcf56b3f963",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Preceded by a specified day such as Sunday, today, or yesterday: a week from (either before or after) the specified day."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "attributive",
                            "obsolete",
                            "poetic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "de50061c-b9a1-4947-9f10-5b75c3abf8ba",
                                "sense_id": "c0d9f480-c8f3-35e2-a0ce-cb216f515b65",
                                "text": ", week last and sevennight"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3898e862-a423-45cd-b334-a619b53a9747",
                                "sense_id": "c0d9f480-c8f3-35e2-a0ce-cb216f515b65",
                                "text": "It will be in my power to assure him that her ladyship was quite well yesterday se'nnight."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "062f71d5-2b95-44ae-bc74-6c97be051d8a",
                                "sense_id": "c0d9f480-c8f3-35e2-a0ce-cb216f515b65",
                                "text": "I was snowed up at a friend's house once for a week. Nothing could be pleasanter. I went for only one night, and could not get away till that very day se'nnight."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "440dcb6b-bbc0-4f5c-a8a7-3116e3bf7052",
                                "sense_id": "c0d9f480-c8f3-35e2-a0ce-cb216f515b65",
                                "text": "We leave Bath, as she has perhaps told you, on Saturday se'nnight."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fe56539-ab02-44ac-922d-14ba13aaea23",
                                "sense_id": "c0d9f480-c8f3-35e2-a0ce-cb216f515b65",
                                "text": "As for his marriage with the Lady Margaret, fixed though it was for this day sennight, the thing was so palpably absurd that he scarcely gave it a thought."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8dbf469b-78cb-3ac1-8d24-e1f8e92dd51d",
                        "entry_id": "7ef50c6c-fdaf-351e-8810-0dcf56b3f963",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Preceded by a specified day and come: a week after the specified day."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1b3c2ae8-5291-4114-94bd-e18f14b99bd2",
                                "sense_id": "8dbf469b-78cb-3ac1-8d24-e1f8e92dd51d",
                                "text": "And Mrs. Jevvkes tells me, every one names Thurſday come Sev'nnight for our Nuptials."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0285208d-2e52-356d-a381-33a738b03f0c",
                        "entry_id": "7ef50c6c-fdaf-351e-8810-0dcf56b3f963",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Preceded by a specified day and gone or was: a week before the specified day."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d1b72f3-27f2-4ff6-9be7-8a66178c20ec",
                                "sense_id": "0285208d-2e52-356d-a381-33a738b03f0c",
                                "text": "Sir Robert Pringle and John Hunter attended the meeting of Heritors intimated here on Sunday gone a se'enight."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
